.TH JOB-SCHEDULER-LAUNCHER 1 "" "job-scheduler" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
job-scheduler-launcher \- start Job Scheduler with administrative privileges
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B job-scheduler-launcher
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B job-scheduler-launcher
is a wrapper used by Job Scheduler to request administrative privileges through
.BR pkexec (1).
It preserves the desktop environment needed by the graphical application and
then starts
.BR job-scheduler (1)
as root.
.PP
Most users should start Job Scheduler from the desktop menu instead of invoking
this wrapper directly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR job-scheduler (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR crontab (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the MX Linux contributors.
